  "generated_text": "To solve the expression \\((x + 1 - x)! \\div (x - x + 1)!\\), we will first simplify the terms inside the factorial expressions.\n\n### Step 1: Simplify the Numerator\nThe numerator is \\((x + 1 - x)!\\). Simplify the expression inside the factorial:\n\\[\nx + 1 - x = 1\n\\]\nThus, the numerator simplifies to:\n\\[\n1!\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Simplify the Denominator\nThe denominator is \\((x - x + 1)!\\). Simplify the expression inside the factorial:\n\\[\nx - x + 1 = 1\n\\]\nThus, the denominator simplifies to:\n\\[\n1!\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Evaluate the Factorials\nNow, we need to evaluate the factorials of 1:\n\\[\n1! = 1\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Perform the Division\nSubstitute the simplified values back into the original expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{1!}{1!} = \\frac{1}{1} = 1\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\nThe value of the expression \\((x + 1 - x)! \\div (x - x + 1)!\\) in simplest form is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
